mpackage = [[Ailo Updater]]
author = [[Ailo]]
title = [[Auto-updater for Ailo's custom Icesus packages]]
description = [[Checks github.com/Ailoman/mudlet-packages on every connect (and every 6 hours while connected) and silently installs newer versions of any package listed in the repo's manifest.lua -- the same self-update pattern the official Icesus core package uses against its own repo. Never touches Icesus's own files or any package not in this repo. Manual check: `aupdate` (reports "everything is up to date" when there's nothing to do).

v4 (2026-09-05): fixed the actual bug behind "aupdate never reports anything, ever" -- readManifest() picked its Lua loader with `local loader = load or loadstring`. Mudlet's Lua 5.1 defines BOTH globals, so `load` always won that `or`, but Lua 5.1's `load(f, chunkname)` only accepts a reader FUNCTION -- handing it the manifest's string content threw "bad argument #1 to 'loader' (function expected, got string)" on every single real download. That error fired inside the sysDownloadDone event handler, which Mudlet logs to its Errors console instead of the main window, so it looked exactly like total silence: no "checking" follow-up, no timeout message (checking correctly cleared to false in the handler's early lines before the crash), nothing. The v3 fix (path-separator normalisation) was real and still needed for the *original* Windows report, but it was never the thing actually reproducing on this machine -- this loader bug was. Swapped to `loadstring or load`, which is the string-accepting form in 5.1 and is what actually needs to run here.]]
version = [[4]]
created = "2026-09-05"